/-!
# Full-kernel bounds from an elementary action image

The elementary-actor calculation of MS93 (3.3) depends on the actor's
image on the natural or augmentation cover. It does not require an
unproved elementary structure on its full inverse image.

Suppose three elementary seeds generate P and [P,P] lies in the first
seed, whose action image is the critical transposition. The derived image
is trivial: it consists of even permutations and lies in the order-two
subgroup generated by an odd transposition. The three elementary images
therefore commute and generate an elementary image. The cover calculation
bounds the full critical-kernel commutator by two and aligns it with the
critical line and full endpoint center. Transport through the actual edge
embedding retains the whole central attachment on both moving covers.

`SixteenEqual` applies this result to the two conjugate backward seeds
and the starting seed. Their full join need not be abelian.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher, Pushing up weak BN-pairs of rank two
(1993), (3.3)(ii)(2) and (5.7), printed pp.866--867 and 919.
-/

public noncomputable section
